ut like really  preparing  and then letting it go when you get on  set and just trying to live in it  speaking of the camera mickey do you and  mac just have it  all down to a science at this point or  is there anything drastically different  about your collaboration on this one  um no i mean we're at this point we're  like a a married couple we don't have to  i send him  so many references and i show him my my  little drawings  and then this one we really were able to  talk about okay we know we can  actually map it out for the time of day  now right  uh there's there's moments we talked a  lot about shooting during magic hour and  so  we have this kind of communication and  and the nice thing is is working with  someone for so long  if something does not work or a shot's  just not going to happen  it's like all right let's figure out  exactly the intention and the emotion we  want to  evoke but let's make it practical to  where we're shooting because none of  these  were sets i mean the house that jeremy  lives in was like  was like built in the 1800s it was all  kind of lopsided on the foundation  you get like seasick in there so uh you  know it really was the effort of  communicating and talking through these  real life places  uh so yeah we we've got a great  relationship uh  i can't sing his praises enough  are you ever on set and having a tough  day or running into a challenge and the  two of you look at each other and go  well at least it wasn't as bad as that  day on that film  i will tell you what this movie had the  single hardest day of any film  we shot a whole movie in maine during  the blizzard and this movie had  one of the worst days of weather i think  i've ever  encountered in my life it was like it  was literally like 30 degrees and 30  mile an hour winds and it was dialogue  and  you know the sea breeze kept you know  just hitting us in the face  and a whole time i was like they came  down here i dragged them all down here  if  i show that i'm upset right now or that  i feel like i'm gonna pass  out uh you know it's gonna ruin the  whole vibe and so  we really like i feel like that was like  the ultimate hardship so now  we can look back and be like at least  this wasn't like off season where we all  almost got  swept away by uh by the violent florida  winds  jocelyn and joe if you could go back to  the very beginning of the shoot and give  yourselves one piece of advice as far as  dealing with the elements while filming  what would it be and why  my wardrobe was um actually perfect for  that day i have to say i  um the first day of shooting it was so  hot  and i was just sweating non-stop but the  day that mickey's talking about i was  like  actually quite comfortable i got to be  in the car  i was in a nice warm outfit um  so i i just was um surfing all the  different  um waves of the shoot and that's the  thing about florida it's  very unpredictable um weather and having  lived in  um florida for a period of time when i  was younger  i kind of knew we were walking into an  environment that you know you just kind  of take it on its own  um merit so i was ready for the  ups and downs i i honestly had a great  time  on the set and um that any technical  issues that came along i really thought  this crew was  totally on top of it i was really  impressed by everybody a great energy  and spirit  so i would say to myself um looking back  go do the movie again  i second that um yeah i honestly like no  there were it was such a delightful  shoot to be on  um i and mickey really just gave me a  lot of courage  moving forward you know he you feel  scared to do things that you haven't  done  for instance that that monologue but he  really was just  so encouraging and so supportive so um  i'm gonna take his vibes with me no  matter who i'm working with  bringing up how good this crew was makes  me think of a question that i used to  ask all the time i haven't asked  recently but if you had a name  an unsung hero of this production  because it's like we know you guys we  know the director  but who is just someone who i don't know  helped you out maybe in an unexpected  way  in uh on a tough day of filming oh  uh well i mean everyone everyone the the  the guys who ran the fog machines were  super patient  considering that uh they would short out  that i would  ask for places to be completely  enveloped in fog because i didn't want  to do  too much digital fog and uh and they did  it i  mean and then the other unsung hero to  an ex is always my editor valerie i mean  she  definitely is able to kind of absorb all  the footage and and really take things  that were the intention and really make  them work so in my mind i mean she's  she's the co-author of all of my films  and she definitely  you know especially like the car crash  sequence is a perfect example it's like  that was that song that i really loved  and i had not thought of it  that way to be almost this big musical  moment and then when she cut it together  she's just like why not this and then  i had to beg warner order music to let  me use the song  and it totally worked out um so yeah so  those are the people i think  you know ev everyone you know we're we  have this luxury of it being a small  enough production  that everyone contributes no one's just  sitting around you know  guarding the generator uh and so  everyone  from from you know across the board  really killed it on this film  in addition to jocelyn and joe your  whole supporting ensemble here is  something else from  like richard brake who's just like  perfectly cast in that role but then  also  you have an actor like the one who plays  miss emily who  i looked up on imdb and that this is the  only credit on her page so  what was it like finding the folks to  fill those roles with your casting  director  oh yeah i mean what we definitely wanted  we realized pretty early on that we  wanted  kind of you know the surrounding  characters to be these authentic  you know to feel authentic and feel  florida and you know  really kind of fit that southern gothic  tone and uh yeah april linscott she came  out of nowhere  and she was just so glorious as miss  emily and then  obviously melora i've been such a fan of  hers for  forever i mean she's one of my heroes as  an actor and i  literally i was like please laura  whatever we could do to  make this work i'll do anything and she  was very great  i'm very proud of everybody they just ah  when i can just like worship the actors  that's my dream and everyone crushed it  on this movie  you you should be mighty proud to end  here  i'm kind of bringing back a question for  you mickey that i think i've asked you  in almost every single interview and i  don't even know it's necessarily what  you want but i keep waiting for the day  when you get  just this enormous budget to work with  you're on a studio platform where  everyone out there you get the widest  possible audience for your work  is that anything that could possibly be  on the horizon and if not  what's just the next i guess the next  big step in your craft that you might  want to tackle with a future film  um yeah i mean sure it's definitely i've  i've done a couple  studio projects and scripts that haven't  obviously gone um  but it's very nice to to get paid or to  write a script for a studio  um but i you know i think the directors  that i look towards are someone you know  are the coen brothers or  you know someone like uh joe uh you know  who  kind of worked the way up to get bigger  and bigger and bigger budgets and you  know  bring along this huge ensemble and and  continuously make things to push the  envelope and i think that's the great  thing about this movie is  i always say i want my my movies to look  to make the previous ones look like  postage stamps you know  look the size and poses him and i  definitely feel like this movie  was by the end of it we i poured  everything into it now all i want to do  is make sure that people see how big you  know florida can look on on screen  as much as you are pulling that off i  still quite love everything that came  before this one but  huge congratulations on off season to  all of you for all of our viewers out  there  make sure to keep an eye out for it i  think you're going to dig it and in the  meantime just  i don't know i can't rattle off every  title go search mickey's name on imdb  and pick  any of those films on his filmography  and you are  all set again guys congratulations thank  you so much  thanks barry
 

